{"units": [{"id": "pais-puer-quote4", "translation": "children of old men"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote5", "translation": "a child pursues a winged bird"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote6", "translation": "children who died as if at the hands of their own kin"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote7", "translation": "to moor in the swaddling clothes of a child, like a ship"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote8", "translation": "for a child still in swaddling clothes does not speak"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote9", "translation": "the washer of the child's swaddling clothes"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote10", "translation": "and by the destruction of the seed of children, the strength is ruined"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote11", "translation": "a band of children and women"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote12", "translation": "child, child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote13", "translation": "O child, child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote14", "translation": "child of Themis, steep in counsel"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote15", "translation": "son of Cronus"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote16", "translation": "O son of Cronus"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote17", "translation": "or she will bear a child mightier than his father"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote18", "translation": "or will my son release you from your toils?"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote19", "translation": "making her child her own husband"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote20", "translation": "my child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote21", "translation": "my child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote22", "translation": "for my child and my house"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote23", "translation": "for your child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote24", "translation": "and the child was present"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote25", "translation": "bringing kindly libations for the child to his father"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote26", "translation": "my child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote27", "translation": "his child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote28", "translation": "and the son of Cyrus"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote29", "translation": "he met the child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote30", "translation": "dishonor of the child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote31", "translation": "I will try to meet my child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote32", "translation": "the child of Batanouchus"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote33", "translation": "from these, your child is not standing by here"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote34", "translation": "the sons of Atreus"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote35", "translation": "the child of Alcmene"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote36", "translation": "burning the blood-red brand, the same age as the child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote37", "translation": "the son of Maia"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote38", "translation": "stop, O child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote39", "translation": "children of Hephaestus"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote40", "translation": "child of Zeus"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote41", "translation": "the marriage of the sons of Aegyptus"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote42", "translation": "the fate of the child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote43", "translation": "the child of the cow"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote44", "translation": "son of Apollo"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote45", "translation": "child of Earth"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote46", "translation": "for the sons of Aegyptus"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote47", "translation": "sons of Aegyptus"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote48", "translation": "she bore a blameless child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote49", "translation": "O Zeus, child of Earth"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote50", "translation": "the sons of Aegyptus"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote51", "translation": "son of Atreus"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote52", "translation": "my child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote53", "translation": "my child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote54", "translation": "O child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote55", "translation": "and desire will charm one of the children"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote56", "translation": "how greatly you have blamed the mind of a young child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote57", "translation": "O child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote58", "translation": "old children"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote59", "translation": "or the virgin Justice, child of Zeus"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote60", "translation": "he sacrificed his own child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote61", "translation": "by the perfect Justice of my child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote62", "translation": "another Titaness, child of Earth"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote63", "translation": "child of Olympian Zeus"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote64", "translation": "great, ambitious children of Night"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote65", "translation": "children, you must be wise"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote66", "translation": "take courage, children"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote67", "translation": "O children"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote68", "translation": "children of father Oceanus"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote69", "translation": "and the seven daughters of Atlas"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote70", "translation": "to the Nymphs, the life-giving children of Inachus, the Argive river"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote71", "translation": "and the children of Tethys"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote72", "translation": "take courage, children, nurtured by mothers"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote73", "translation": "O children of the Greeks"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote74", "translation": "and free the children and women"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote75", "translation": "and which of my children commanded the army there?"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote76", "translation": "having a godless spirit toward her children"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote77", "translation": "O children, O saviors of your father's hearth"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote78", "translation": "and it has happened more to the children"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote79", "translation": "send help to the children"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote80", "translation": "for children are saving omens for a man when he is dead"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote81", "translation": "sacrifices on behalf of the children and the marriage rite"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote82", "translation": "city-protecting children of Cranaus"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote83", "translation": "these things remain for the children and the house"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote84", "translation": "they are torn by the voiceless children of the undefiled one"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote85", "translation": "in the manner of vultures, which with out-of-the-way griefs for their children – they whirl about"}, {"id": "pais-puer-quote86", "translation": "for he will show two forms, of the child and of himself, from one womb"}, {"id": "pais-puer-word1", "translation": "to rush"}, {"id": "pais-puer-word2", "translation": "for my child"}, {"id": "pais-puer-word3", "translation": "children"}, {"id": "pais-puer-word4", "translation": "children"}, {"id": "pais-puer-word5", "translation": "of the sea"}, {"id": "paio-orth1", "translation": "to strike"}, {"id": "paio-def1", "translation": "to strike, to smite"}, {"id": "paio-def2", "translation": "passive"}, {"id": "paio-note1", "translation": "where the scholiast says: \"disturbed words, as they happen, dash against the wave of evils, that is, under pain they speak much.\""}, {"id": "paio-note2", "translation": "[παίσας [having struck] in the scholia to Pindar for πταίσας [having stumbled]. See πταίω.]"}]}